| Pattern | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `Rc<T>` | Multiple owners of a node; no lifetime tracking needed. |
| `RefCell<T>` | Allows `borrow()` / `borrow_mut()` at **runtime** instead of compile time. |
| `Weak<T>` | For the `prev` pointer. If both directions were `Rc`, nodes would keep each other alive forever (memory leak). `Weak` breaks the cycle; it can be `upgrade()`d back to an `Rc` only while the forward direction still exists. |
| `clone()` on `Rc` | Increases the reference count. The compiler never asks “how long does this live?” because the data lives as long as any `Rc` points to it. |

