The standard Rust idiom for cyclic, mutable graphs is:
- **`Rc<T>`** for shared ownership (no lifetimes needed because ownership is reference-counted).
- **`RefCell<T>`** for interior mutability (borrows are checked at *runtime*, not compile-time).
